{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 2, :comments ["<b>Men of renown, those called to the assembly.</b> It appears that men of stubborn heart, lovers of excess honor and dominion, gathered to Korah — reckoning that he would give offices of authority to all of them, for this is the thing that the soul of every man of name sought, those who said among themselves, 'Let us make ourselves a name, lest we become a disgrace.' And the beginning of their words proves this: ״רַב לָכֶם״ and so on, for they said: it is justice that dominion should rotate continually from one to another, for 'it is too much for you' — many days have you exercised dominion over Israel; and it is fitting that you should give the tribe of governance into the hands of others, ״כִּי כָל הָעֵדָה כֻלָּם קְדֹשִׁים״. And ״כֻלָּם״ is superfluous; rather, this is what they said: it is known that an עֵדָה is no fewer than ten, and in every assembly throughout Israel — all of them are holy; every assembly, on its own, possesses holiness, for nothing involving holiness is found in fewer than ten, for in every assembly of ten there is holiness, וּבְתוֹכָם ה׳. And you — it is not enough that you exalt yourselves over an assembly of ten, but you exalt yourselves even over the entire congregation of HaShem, and this thing is insufferable. And therefore he began with ״עֵדָה״ and concluded with ״קָהָל״, to say that even if you were exalting yourselves over an assembly of ten, we would have grounds to complain against you — for behold, every assembly possesses holiness; all the more so is there cause to complain, ״מַדּוּעַ תִּתְנַשְּׂאוּ עַל קְהַל ה׳״, over all of them as one. And as for what they said, ״וּבְתוֹכָם ה׳״ — for in every place where you find the greatness of the Holy One, blessed be He, there you find His humility (Megillah 31a), and behold the Holy One, blessed be He, shows humility toward Israel and walks בְּתוֹכָם, that is to say, in the middle and not at the head, to say: I am to you like a friend, like a brother, and I do not seek to go at the head as is My right — and how is it that you exalt yourselves over the congregation of HaShem?"], :book :numbers, :voice :kli-yakar, :lang :en, :chapter 16, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T13:41:29.852489595Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}